   <narrative xml:lang="EN">INTERVENTIONS TO STRENGTHEN COMMUNITY&amp;PRIMARY HEAL CARE SYSTM FOR REPROD,MATERN&amp;N</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of Mkapa Fellows phase five programme is to improve Health and Community Systems and Services for addressing maternal, newborn, child and adolescent health challenges in Dodoma region in Tanzania. The programme works to strengthen human resources for health, including community health workers, through deployment and capacity development while collaborating with the Irish Health Service Executive to strengthen quality of primary healthcare services. It builds health system Resilience to adapt to climate shocks including Climate sensitive diseases.</narrative>
  </description>
